IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `spr-part2-prisoners`

-- Tests for Part 2 (regulations 2 and 3). Expected values are written from the text (lines 28 to 44).

§ `Part 2`

§§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of custody`
      `in GB` IS A BOOLEAN
      similar IS A BOOLEAN
      certified IS A MAYBE DATE
      remanded IS A BOOLEAN
      later IS A MAYBE `Sentence imposed`
GIVETH A `A day of a person's custody`
`a day of custody` kind `in GB` similar certified remanded later MEANS
    `A day of a person's custody` WITH
        `the day` IS Date 10 6 2026
        `the kind of custody` IS kind
        `in Great Britain` IS `in GB`
        `in similar circumstances in Great Britain the person would not have been a prisoner` IS similar
        `the release date the Secretary of State has certified` IS certified
        `remanded in custody for an offence` IS remanded
        `the sentence later imposed for that offence` IS later

GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of sentence`
      outside IS A BOOLEAN
      similar IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Sentence imposed`
`a sentence` kind outside similar MEANS
    `Sentence imposed` WITH
        `its kind` IS kind
        `it was imposed outside Great Britain` IS outside
        `in similar circumstances in Great Britain a sentence of imprisonment or detention would not have been imposed` IS similar

`criminal custody` MEANS `imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings`
`at large` MEANS `unlawfully at large`
`section 47` MEANS `detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983`
`section 136` MEANS `detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003`
`other custody` MEANS `in none of those kinds of custody`

`imprisonment` MEANS `a sentence of imprisonment or detention in legal custody as a result of criminal proceedings`
`mental health detention` MEANS `a sentence of detention where the provisions mentioned in regulation 2(2)(c)(i) or (d) apply`
`suspended sentence` MEANS `a suspended sentence within the meaning in section 286 of the Sentencing Code`
`other sentence` MEANS `a sentence of none of those kinds`

§§ `Regulation 2(2)(a) and (b), and 2(3)`

-- (a) a prisoner in Great Britain or elsewhere imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with criminal proceedings.
#ASSERT `the person is a prisoner within regulation 2(2) on the day` (`a day of custody` `criminal custody` TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING)
#ASSERT `the person is a prisoner within regulation 2(2) on the day` (`a day of custody` `criminal custody` FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING)
-- (3) outside Great Britain, and in similar circumstances in Great Britain the person would not have been a prisoner: not a prisoner.
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is a prisoner within regulation 2(2) on the day` (`a day of custody` `criminal custody` FALSE TRUE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING))
-- (3) does not reach a person in Great Britain, even if the same flag is set.
#ASSERT `the person is a prisoner within regulation 2(2) on the day` (`a day of custody` `criminal custody` TRUE TRUE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING)
#ASSERT `paragraph (3) of regulation 2 applies on the day` (`a day of custody` `criminal custody` FALSE TRUE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`paragraph (3) of regulation 2 applies on the day` (`a day of custody` `criminal custody` TRUE TRUE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING))
-- (b) a prisoner in Great Britain or elsewhere who is unlawfully at large.
#ASSERT `the person is a prisoner within regulation 2(2) on the day` (`a day of custody` `at large` TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING)
#ASSERT `the person is a prisoner within regulation 2(2) on the day` (`a day of custody` `at large` FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is a prisoner within regulation 2(2) on the day` (`a day of custody` `at large` FALSE TRUE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING))

§§ `Regulation 2(2)(c) and (d): in Great Britain only`

-- (c): in Great Britain, detained under section 47, on or before the day the Secretary of State certifies as the release date (if any).
#ASSERT `the person is a prisoner within regulation 2(2) on the day` (`a day of custody` `section 47` TRUE FALSE (JUST (Date 11 6 2026)) FALSE NOTHING)
-- "on or before": the day itself is included.
#ASSERT `the person is a prisoner within regulation 2(2) on the day` (`a day of custody` `section 47` TRUE FALSE (JUST (Date 10 6 2026)) FALSE NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is a prisoner within regulation 2(2) on the day` (`a day of custody` `section 47` TRUE FALSE (JUST (Date 9 6 2026)) FALSE NOTHING))
-- No certified date: the text says "(if any)"; fork F4 takes the condition as met.
#ASSERT `the person is a prisoner within regulation 2(2) on the day` (`a day of custody` `section 47` TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING)
-- (c) is for a prisoner in Great Britain; (d) likewise.
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is a prisoner within regulation 2(2) on the day` (`a day of custody` `section 47` FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING))
#ASSERT `the person is a prisoner within regulation 2(2) on the day` (`a day of custody` `section 136` TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is a prisoner within regulation 2(2) on the day` (`a day of custody` `section 136` FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING))
-- Not in custody of any kind in paragraph (2).
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is a prisoner within regulation 2(2) on the day` (`a day of custody` `other custody` TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING))

§§ `Regulation 2(1): the state pension is not to be paid for a day on which the person is a prisoner`

#ASSERT `a state pension is not to be paid for the day` (`a day of custody` `criminal custody` TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`a state pension is not to be paid for the day` (`a day of custody` `other custody` TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING))
#ASSERT NOT (`a state pension is not to be paid for the day` (`a day of custody` `criminal custody` FALSE TRUE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING))

§§ `Regulation 3(1): remanded in custody`

-- A person remanded in custody, with no sentence later imposed: regulation 2(1) does not apply.
#ASSERT `regulation 2(1) does not apply to the day because of regulation 3` (`a day of custody` `criminal custody` TRUE FALSE NOTHING TRUE NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`a state pension is not to be paid for the day` (`a day of custody` `criminal custody` TRUE FALSE NOTHING TRUE NOTHING))
-- Not on remand: regulation 3 does not displace regulation 2(1).
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 2(1) does not apply to the day because of regulation 3` (`a day of custody` `criminal custody` TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING))

§§ `Regulation 3(2): the sentences that bring regulation 2(1) back`

-- (a) imprisonment or detention in legal custody as a result of criminal proceedings.
#ASSERT `a state pension is not to be paid for the day` (`a day of custody` `criminal custody` TRUE FALSE NOTHING TRUE (JUST (`a sentence` `imprisonment` FALSE FALSE)))
-- (b) a sentence of detention where regulation 2(2)(c)(i) or (d) applies.
#ASSERT `a state pension is not to be paid for the day` (`a day of custody` `criminal custody` TRUE FALSE NOTHING TRUE (JUST (`a sentence` `mental health detention` FALSE FALSE)))
-- (c) a suspended sentence.
#ASSERT `a state pension is not to be paid for the day` (`a day of custody` `criminal custody` TRUE FALSE NOTHING TRUE (JUST (`a sentence` `suspended sentence` FALSE FALSE)))
-- A sentence of none of the described kinds does not bring regulation 2(1) back.
#ASSERT NOT (`a state pension is not to be paid for the day` (`a day of custody` `criminal custody` TRUE FALSE NOTHING TRUE (JUST (`a sentence` `other sentence` FALSE FALSE))))

§§ `Regulation 3(3): a sentence of kind (2)(a) imposed outside Great Britain`

-- Imposed outside Great Britain and, in similar circumstances in Great Britain, no such sentence would have been imposed: not a described sentence.
#ASSERT NOT (`the sentence is one described in regulation 3(2)` (`a sentence` `imprisonment` TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a state pension is not to be paid for the day` (`a day of custody` `criminal custody` FALSE FALSE NOTHING TRUE (JUST (`a sentence` `imprisonment` TRUE TRUE))))
-- Imposed outside Great Britain but one would have been imposed in Great Britain: described.
#ASSERT `the sentence is one described in regulation 3(2)` (`a sentence` `imprisonment` TRUE FALSE)
-- Imposed in Great Britain: the flag is not read.
#ASSERT `the sentence is one described in regulation 3(2)` (`a sentence` `imprisonment` FALSE TRUE)
-- Paragraph (3) speaks only of a sentence described in paragraph (2)(a): kinds (b) and (c) are untouched.
#ASSERT `the sentence is one described in regulation 3(2)` (`a sentence` `mental health detention` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the sentence is one described in regulation 3(2)` (`a sentence` `suspended sentence` TRUE TRUE)

§§ `Regulation 2(4)`

-- Regulation 13 shall not have effect when determining rights to relevant benefits for regulation 2.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 13 has effect when determining rights to relevant benefits for regulation 2`)
